===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or relating to the [[Bible]].
#: {{ux|en|Tithing is both a quranic and '''biblical''' virtue.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author={{w|Margery Allingham}}|title={{w|The China Governess}}|chapter=3|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W|passage=Sepia Delft tiles surrounded the fireplace, their crudely drawn '''Biblical''' scenes in faded cyclamen blending with the pinkish pine, while above them, instead of a mantelshelf, there was an archway high enough to form a balcony with slender balusters and a tapestry-hung wall behind.}}
# In accordance with the [[teaching]]s of the Bible (according to some interpretation of it).
#: {{ux|en|The biblical teaching is that{{...}}}}
#: {{ux|en|'''biblical''' morality}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Chris McGreal|quotee=Mike Pompeo|title=Pompeo says Israel has biblical claim to Palestine and is ‘not an occupying nation’|work=The Guardian|date=2023-02-16|url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/16/mike-pompeo-israel-biblical-claim-palestine-not-occupying|issn=0261-3077|passage=Mike Pompeo, the former US secretary of state, has defended Israel’s decades-long control of the Palestinian territories by claiming that the Jewish state has a '''biblical''' claim to the land and is therefore not occupying it.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Very [[great]]; especially, [[exceeding]] previous [[records]] in [[scale]].
#: {{ux|en|of '''biblical''' proportions}}
#: {{ux|en|with '''biblical''' fury}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1984|writers={{w|Dan Aykroyd}}; {{w|Harold Ramis}}|title={{w|Ghostbusters}}|passage=Dr. Peter Venkman: This city is headed for a disaster of '''biblical''' proportions.<br/>Mayor: What do you mean, "'''biblical'''"?<br/>Dr. Raymond Stantz: What he means is Old Testament, Mr. Mayor, real wrath-of-God type stuff.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.nytimes.com/books/98/02/22/reviews/980222.22kirnlt.html|title=The Wages of Righteousness|date=1998-02-22|work=The New York Times|author=Walter Kirn|passage=Russell Banks's “Cloudsplitter,” a novel of near-'''biblical''' proportions about the abolitionist freedom fighter John Brown, is shaped like an                explosive with an exceedingly long and winding fuse.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Damian Carrington|quotee=António Guterres|title=Rising seas threaten ‘mass exodus on a biblical scale’, UN chief warns|work=The Guardian|date=2023-02-14|url=https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/feb/14/rising-seas-threaten-mass-exodus-on-a-biblical-scale-un-chief-warns|issn=0261-3077|passage=An increase in the pace at which sea levels are rising threatens “a mass exodus of entire populations on a '''biblical''' scale”, the UN secretary general has warned.}}

